From: zortos293 <65777760+zortos293@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:27:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] video_core: shader stores still queued keep an equal or
 mask acquire draining

They are placed nowhere and mark their pages GPU-written only once the back runs
them, so a settled word now also needs the back past every cache write sent
(after its note, if one is queued), and is checked for GPU-written pages after
that. Review finding on #2143.

(cherry picked from commit a4711afdf29a14f87cb016eac78e22535b22391e)
---
 src/tests/video_core/maxwell_fast_method.cpp | 34 +++++++++++++++++++-
 src/video_core/gpu_split.cpp                 | 26 ++++++++-------
 src/video_core/gpu_split.h                   |  7 ++--
 3 files changed, 51 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

